# Filter styles

Every **filter** control in the app — toolbar filter chips, segmented source
filters, engine/date chips, dropdown menus inside those chips, Advanced filter
trigger + Clear, and Advanced filter drawer field/operator selects and footer
actions — uses **14px** text.

## Fixed typography — never change

- Filter chip labels: `text-[14px] font-medium`
- Filter chip value badges (e.g. `All`, `ChatGPT`): `text-[14px]`
- Filter dropdown menu items: `text-[14px]`
- Advanced filter trigger label + Clear: `text-[14px]`
- Advanced filter drawer selects / actions: `text-[14px]`

## Exceptions

- The **numeric count badge** on the active Advanced filter trigger stays
  `text-[12px]` (compact circular badge).
- Table body status pills (HTTP codes, Yes/No, etc.) are not filters — keep the
  12px badge floor.

## Shared pieces

- Advanced filter trigger: `src/components/AdvancedFilterTrigger.jsx`
- Advanced filter drawer: `src/components/AdvancedFilterDrawer.jsx`

## Do not

- Use `text-[13px]` or `text-[12px]` for filter chip labels, menus, or Clear.
- Fork a smaller type scale per dashboard toolbar.
